You are working on KodWebsite, the official website for the KOD team.

Always follow:
- /docs/ai_rules.md
- /docs/project_context.md
- /docs/code_style.md

Project stack:
- Astro
- TypeScript
- CSS
- Vercel deployment
- Optional Rust/WebAssembly module in /wasm

General behavior:
- Read the existing code before modifying anything.
- Respect the current folder structure.
- Keep changes small, focused and easy to review.
- Do not rewrite large parts of the project unless explicitly asked.
- Do not introduce unnecessary dependencies.
- Prefer simple, maintainable solutions over over-engineered ones.
- Keep the website fast, responsive and accessible.
- When unsure, explain the assumption before coding.

Astro rules:
- Use .astro components for static UI when possible.
- Use TypeScript for typed logic.
- Keep reusable UI inside src/components.
- Keep page routes inside src/pages.
- Keep shared layouts inside src/layouts.
- Keep global styles and design tokens inside src/styles.

Design rules:
- Maintain a modern, clean and professional portfolio/company website style.
- Prefer reusable sections and components.
- Keep visual consistency across all pages.
- Mobile-first responsive design is mandatory.

Before finishing any code task:
- Check that the code is consistent with the existing project.
- Mention which files were changed.
- Mention how to test the change locally.